1
00:00:00,119 --> 00:00:04,720
This wouldn't be a youtube channel without
a cat video - so without further ado, we present:

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:05,720
Schrodinger's cat.

3
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:09,310
I'm sure you've heard some version of this
famous thought experiment: you put a cat in

4
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:12,929
a bunker with some unstable gunpowder that
has a 50% chance of blowing up in the next

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:15,150
minute, and 50% chance of doing nothing.

6
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:20,800
[the gunpowder is Einstein's version - Schrodinger
preferred poisonous gas] So until we look

7
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:25,231
in the bunker, we don't know whether the cat
is dead or alive, and when we do look, it

8
00:00:25,231 --> 00:00:26,950
is either dead or alive.

9
00:00:26,950 --> 00:00:31,520
But if we repeat the experiment enough times
with enough cats and bunkers and gunpowder,

10
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:35,379
we'll see that half the time kitty survives,
and half the time kitty goes bye-bye.

11
00:00:35,379 --> 00:00:40,160
The quantum mechanical interpretation is that
before we look, the cat is in a superposition

12
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:44,940
- it's both dead AND alive - and our act of
looking forces nature's decision.

13
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,989
So our curiosity kills the cat.

14
00:00:46,989 --> 00:00:48,710
But what about the cat's perspective?

15
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:53,510
Well, the cat either sees the gunpowder explode,
or not – so inside the bunker we actually

16
00:00:53,510 --> 00:00:57,539
have these two possibilities: "the powder
exploded and the cat saw it explode" or "the

17
00:00:57,539 --> 00:01:00,499
powder didn't explode and the cat didn't see
it explode".

18
00:01:00,499 --> 00:01:04,740
There's no option: "the powder exploded and
the cat didn't see it explode" - so the cat's

19
00:01:04,740 --> 00:01:07,740
reality becomes entangled with the outcome
of the experiment!

20
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:11,820
And it's our observation of the experiment
that forces nature to "collapse" to one option

21
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:13,430
or the other.

22
00:01:13,430 --> 00:01:18,270
But we're like the cat, too – either the
cat dies and we see it dead, or the cat lives

23
00:01:18,270 --> 00:01:23,290
and we see it alive – so who's observing
us to force nature to "collapse" to one reality?

24
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:27,540
Or do both possibilities happen in parallel
within a larger multiverse?

25
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:31,720
This "collapsing to one reality" problem is
one of the biggest unanswered questions in

26
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:32,880
quantum physics.

27
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:45,790
So for kitty's sake, can i has answer pleez?
